STAT3D intermediate results :
"z_slice_measurement.csv" file. This file idenfies how many z-stacks are in each level of the image pyramid
"export" folder. This folder shows the image of every z-stack in the "morphology.ome.tif" image.The images can be inspected with software applications such as QuPath. The images will help the users in the choice of the most accurate two z-stacks to consider as Z_stack_A and Z_stack_B. The quantification of the images resolution is provided in the Laplacian_score.csv file.
"Laplacian_score.csv". This file indicates the level of sharpness of the first 10 images (z0,z1,z2,...z9) that form the z-stack in the "morphology.ome.tif" image
"QuPath_measurements.csv". This file contains all the image's information regarding the size and area of the nuclei detected in the tissue biopsy. It represents the base for the nuclei average diameter and nuclear expansion average calculations
"nuclei_diameter.csv". This file represents the value of the average diameter of the nuclei in the tissue biopsy. It will be automatically implemented in the Cellpose segmentation.
"average_min_distance.csv". This file represent the average minimum distance across the nuclei. It is used during the calculation of the average nuclear expansion value.
"average_nuclear_expansion.csv". This file represent the epansion of each nuclei to ensure correct transcripts assignation and avoid overlap with proximal cells.
"feature.tsv". This file represents the TSV format of the gene list needed for the generation of the Seurat objects. It is subsequently gzipped (features.tsv.gz) by the pipeline to obtain the correct Seurat object via the function Read10x.
"barcodes.tsv". This file represents the TSV format of the cell locations in X,Y,Z coordinates for every cell ("cell_id").It is subsequently gzipped (barcodes.tsv.gz) by the pipeline to obtain the correct Seurat object via the function Read10x.
"matrix.mtx". This file represents the TSV format of the matrix market exchange(.mxt). It contains the number of transcripts for each gene detected within each segmented cell in a tissue sample.It is subsequently gzipped (barcodes.tsv.gz) by the pipeline to obtain the correct Seurat object via the function Read10x.
"QuPath_script". Groovy script autogenerated by STAT3D. Its output is the "QuPath_measurements.csv" file. It is automatically saved in the workflow folder.
"Z_slice_script". Groovy script autogenerated by STAT3D. Its output is the "z_slice_measurement.csv" file. It is automatically saved in the workflow folder.
